# Carrier-BSP env consumed by stone-provision-tegraflash.sh.
#
# Advantech MIC-712-OX — Jetson Orin NX SOM (P3767-0000, 16GB) on Advantech's
# P3768-class carrier. The factory image flashes the stock NVIDIA
# `jetson-orin-nano-devkit-super` profile (board_sku 0000, "super" mode),
# then overlays Advantech's carrier customizations. This extension layers
# onto the generic `jetson-orin-nx` MACHINE and redirects the flash flow at
# the Advantech-modified files below.
#
# Files differing from stock L4T R36.4.3 were taken straight from the
# extracted Advantech BSP (MIC-712_OrinNX_6.2.0_V1.0.3) and renamed with an
# `-adv` suffix to make their carrier origin explicit vs. the stock NVIDIA
# filenames the MACHINE bakes. The Advantech deltas (by mtime in the BSP:
# Aug 2025 vs. the Jan 2025 stock files) are exactly two MB1 BCT files plus
# the kernel DTB:
#   * tegra234-mb1-bct-pinmux-p3767-hdmi-a03-adv.dtsi  (67 KB; carrier pin
#     routing for the 7x Intel igb NICs behind the ASMedia PCIe switch, the
#     2x mttcan controllers, the isolated RS-232/422/485 transceivers, and
#     the IP808 PoE SMBus select). #includes the -adv gpio dtsi below.
#   * tegra234-mb1-bct-gpio-p3767-hdmi-a03-adv.dtsi    (boot GPIO defaults)
#   * tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767-0000-nv-super-adv.dtb  (kernel DTB; adds the
#     3x ti,tca9554 expanders on i2c0/1/7, the realtek,rt5640 audio codec,
#     ti,ina3221, and the 2x mttcan nodes on top of the stock super DTB).
# padvoltage is stock (unchanged from L4T) and is shipped only so the
# pinmux/gpio #include chain resolves entirely within this overlay.
#
# Flash profile: `flash.sh jetson-orin-nano-devkit-super internal` in
# Advantech's SOP. See meta-avocado-nvidia/docs/adding-a-jetson-carrier.md
# for the full CARRIER_FV_/CARRIER_ENV_ knob reference, and
# bsp/icam-540/stone/carrier-bsp/carrier.env for another Orin NX carrier.

CARRIER_LABEL="Advantech MIC-712-OX (Jetson Orin NX P3767-0000 16GB SOM, P3768 carrier, super mode)"

# Kernel DTB — Advantech's modified super DTB carrying the carrier I/O nodes.
# Flashed via the initrd-flash .env (DTBFILE), matching bsp/icam-540.
CARRIER_ENV_DTBFILE="tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767-0000-nv-super-adv.dtb"

# ODMDATA — UPHY lane map. THE carrier-defining flash parameter. The generic
# jetson-orin-nx MACHINE defaults to gbe-uphy-config-8 (GBE UPHY -> 4x MGBE, the
# Orin NX devkit layout). The MIC-712-OX instead routes the GBE UPHY to PCIe
# C10 (pcie@141e0000) for the ASMedia ASM1806 switch + 6x I350 -> that is
# gbe-uphy-config-9 (the value Advantech's p3767.conf.common sets). Without this
# override MB1 never powers C10's GBE UPHY lanes, and UEFI/BL31 walking the
# unpowered p2u_gbe_1 block (phy@3f30000) trips a fatal RAS UE at boot:
#   RAS Uncorrectable Error in IOB ... ADDR = 0x...3f300c0  ->  core powered off.
# (The 4x MGBE nodes are disabled in our DTB, so config-9 / C10 is correct.)
# Patches ODMDATA= in .env.initrd-flash, which initrd-flash feeds to
# tegraflash --odmdata. Version-independent (T234 ODM lane-config selector).
CARRIER_ENV_ODMDATA="gbe-uphy-config-9,hsstp-lane-map-3,hsio-uphy-config-0"

# BPMP DTB + firmware — "super" board_sku-0000 variant (unlocks MAXN-SUPER
# clocks). The base jetson-orin-nx MACHINE bakes the *non*-super defaults, so
# we ship the super BPMP DTB here and point the flashvar at it. BPF firmware
# blob TE980M matches this SOM's chip SKU (DEFAULT_CHIP_SKU 00:00:00:D3 ->
# bpmp_fw_binary[D3]=TE980M-A1 per p3767.conf.common).
CARRIER_FV_BPFDTB_FILE="tegra234-bpmp-3767-0000-3768-super.dtb"
CARRIER_FV_BPF_FILE="bpmp_t234-TE980M-A1_prod.bin"

# Pinmux + pad-voltage dtsi — HDMI a03 family (the variant p3509-a02 /
# p3768-a0 select for sku 0000). The pinmux is Advantech-modified; padvoltage
# is stock-for-parity. The pinmux #includes the -adv gpio dtsi.
CARRIER_FV_PINMUX_CONFIG="tegra234-mb1-bct-pinmux-p3767-hdmi-a03-adv.dtsi"
CARRIER_FV_PMC_CONFIG="tegra234-mb1-bct-padvoltage-p3767-hdmi-a03-adv.dtsi"

# EEPROM-comparison values — accept the Orin NX 16GB SOM (P3767-0000).
# tegraflash aborts if the SOM EEPROM's boardid/boardsku don't match. Pinning
# these fails fast if a different Orin NX/Nano SKU module is misloaded with
# the MIC-712-OX BSP (e.g. a 8GB 0003 or 4GB 0004).
CARRIER_FV_CHECK_BOARDID="3767"
CARRIER_FV_CHECK_BOARDSKU="0000"
